PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C. Fool

The Book of the Duchess is written in octosyllabic couplets and contains multiple attested rhyme-pairs involving A (wente/hente, stente), B (here/there, were), D (hool/cool, etc.), and E (countour/sour, errour). No line in the poem places "fool" in a rhyming position with any other word, so it is the only item among the choices that Chaucer does not use as a rhyme.}

}

